5. Bundled binaries and rootfs (IMPORTANT — these ARE in the tree)
------------------------------------------------------------------
  Heracles-taixu-sandbox is an **offline, self-contained** sandbox: it must
  work with no network, no server and no cloud. Therefore the following
  third-party artefacts are **included in this repository** (not fetched at
  build time).

  5.1 PRoot runtime — GPL-2.0-or-later
      Files, in sandbox-runtime/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/:

        libproot.so           239,368 B  PRoot tracer (AArch64 executable,
                                         not a JNI library)
        libproot-loader.so     18,136 B  PRoot tracee loader
        libtalloc.so           31,440 B  dynamic dependency of PRoot
        libandroid-shmem.so    14,432 B  dynamic dependency of PRoot

      Copyright (C) 2015-2024 STMicroelectronics and Termux PRoot
      contributors. Licensed under GNU GPL version 2 or later.

      **GPL-2.0 obligation**: because we redistribute these binaries, the
      corresponding source must also be available. Upstream sources:
        - PRoot:            https://github.com/termux/proot
        - talloc:           https://talloc.samba.org/
        - libandroid-shmem: https://github.com/termux/libandroid-shmem

      If you fork and redistribute a binary build of this sandbox you inherit
      this obligation. Shipping this repository (source + these binaries)
      together with the upstream links above is the intended compliance path.
      **Do not delete this section.**

      Note: libproot.so has been binary-patched so that its DT_NEEDED entry
      for talloc reads "libtalloc.so" instead of "libtalloc.so.2", because
      Android APK packaging only permits lib*.so names. This is a load-path
      adaptation, not a functional change; the talloc code is unmodified.
      See docs/integration-guide.md §4.

  5.2 Bundled rootfs — Alpine Linux 3.20 minirootfs
      File: sandbox-runtime/src/main/assets/rootfs-bundle.tar.gz (3,947,906 B)

      This is the official Alpine Linux aarch64 minirootfs
      (alpine-minirootfs-3.20.3-aarch64.tar.gz), obtained unmodified from
      https://alpinelinux.org / its mirrors.

      It contains Alpine packages (busybox, musl libc, apk-tools and their
      dependencies). Each carries its own upstream license — predominantly
      GPL-2.0, MIT and BSD variants. License metadata ships inside the image
      (/lib/apk/db/installed) and at https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org.
      Alpine Linux is not affiliated with this project.

  5.3 Optional: rootfs images pulled via installRootfs(ociRef)
      installRootfs() is an **optional upgrade path**; the bundled rootfs is
      the default. Images pulled this way are NOT in this repository, and the
      license of the referenced distribution applies (e.g. Alpine, Debian).

  5.4 Optional: toolchains installed inside the rootfs
      Their own upstream licenses apply. None are included here.


6. Security boundary of everything above
-----------------------------------------
  None of these bundled artefacts makes this sandbox a security boundary.
  **PRoot provides no namespace / cgroup / seccomp isolation.** It solves
  filesystem pollution and crash recovery, not untrusted-code isolation.
  See docs/security-boundary.md — that statement must not be removed.
